// Puzzle data for Sweep, the daily minesweeper with no bottom edge. Imported
// ONLY by the server page (app/sweep/page.js), which filters live<=today before
// handing the bank to the client, so no future day's field is ever in a page.
//
// A row is the day's frame plus its field:
//
//   par    the day's BENCHMARK cell count, not a ceiling. Cells uncovered are
//          the score: it is the thing you actually do, every player digs the
//          same field, and unlike a timer it cannot be padded by sitting still.
//          The posted score is the raw count, UNCAPPED, and par is only the
//          denominator daily-combined uses for its completion ratio (it clamps
//          at 1, so digging past par is safe and still separates players on
//          placement). Clearing par wins the end card. Sunday's par is lower
//          because the same field carries more mines.
//
//          SET BLIND at launch, exactly as Blocks' were, and expected to be
//          WRONG. 120 is roughly fifteen rows on a weekday field. Revisit both
//          numbers once a fortnight of real scores exists, and expect them to
//          RISE as players learn to read the strip.
//
//   field  the mine map: 9 columns x 200 rows of one bit, base64'd, about 300
//          characters. Depth 200 is not a bottom, it is ~1,500 safe cells and
//          an order of magnitude past par.
//
// EVERY FIELD IS PROVEN GUESS-FREE BEFORE IT SHIPS. A run is one life, so a
// board that forced a guess would end a run through no fault of the player.
// scripts/gen-sweep-bank.mjs builds each field against the solver in
// lib/sweep-field and repairs it until the whole thing is deducible from the
// surface row down; scripts/verify-sweep.mjs re-proves all of it through that
// same module rather than trusting this comment. Never hand-edit a field: it
// would not be re-proven, and the guarantee is the entire design.
//
// SUNDAY EDITION, through 2026-10-25 only: density rose from 15% to 18.5% on
// Sundays. From 2026-10-26 Arcade plays the same every day (owner, 2026-10-25),
// so `sunday` is true on the Sundays up to then and nowhere else; the flag is
// the ONLY source of truth for the badge (see lib/sunday-editions.js).
